# negative seed.
#
# Scenario: a capability cell application is lowered into the reference VM
# with the wrong argument shape (a scalar where the cell contract declares
# a rank-1 vector) and the VM silently coerces / evaluates a partial
# result instead of refusing. A VM that silently succeeds here would ship
# "partial authority": a value computed outside the cell's declared
# contract, indistinguishable from a correct run.
#
# expect: E-VM-APPLY-SHAPE / E-CELL-006 - the reference VM refuses with a
# typed fault (type confusion / capability-layer contract refusal) at the
# apply seam; resource exhaustion and unsupported dispatch are also typed
# refusals (BudgetExhausted / ProviderCallRequired), never partial
# authority and never a silent identity.
use std.kinds.capability

emath capability Softmax:
    class: pure
    version: 1.0.0
    migration: frozen
    inputs:
        x: Float64
    outputs:
        probability: Float64
    definitions:
        probability = softmax(x as Float64)
